# .gitignore — AI-OS repo
# Do not commit:
# - Generated artifacts
# - Generated outputs
# - Dotfile backups
# - User-specific outputs

# Outputs. Two locations on purpose, and the split is the framework/product split:
#   outputs/            — the framework's own artifacts (research reports, audits, diagrams)
#   apps/data/outputs/  — the plans product's run artifacts (enrichment reports, slice
#                         manifests, pipeline logs), written by apps/data/tools/plans-pipeline
# Both are generated and machine-local, so both are ignored with their .gitkeep preserved.
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
apps/data/outputs/*
!apps/data/outputs/.gitkeep

# OS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Dotfile backups generated by setup scripts
.zshrc.pre-aios.bak
.zshrc.pre-oh-my-zsh
.zshrc.pre-omz.bak.*
.p10k.zsh.pre-aios.bak
.gitconfig.pre-aios.bak
.gitignore_global.pre-aios.bak
.config.yaml.pre-aios.bak
.config.yaml.pre-omz.bak.*
.ssh/config.pre-aios.bak

# Claude / Hermes pre-aios backups
.claude/skills/*.pre-aios.bak
.codex/skills/*.pre-aios.bak
.gemini/skills/*.pre-aios.bak
.agents/skills/*.pre-aios.bak
.hermes/skills/imported/*.pre-aios.bak
.hermes/config.yaml.pre-aios.bak

# Local configs
.env
.env.local
*.local
*.log

# Unified env dossier with real secrets (generated locally, never versioned)
dev-env/env-config/env.ts
dev-env/env-config/env-reference.html
# Local zip backup of the env-config dossier (contains real secrets)
dev-env/env-config.zip
# Timestamped copies taken before editing the master .env — same secrets, no protection
.env.bak-*

# Project-local Hermes runtime (may contain real secrets, e.g. desktop-attachments/env.ts)
.hermes/

# Local CLI runtime state (settings.local.json, caches, etc.) — never commit.
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`, because git cannot re-include a file from an
# excluded directory: with the directory form, the negation below is silently dead.
.claude/*
# launch.json is the exception: it is the dev-server contract (which app, which port),
# it holds no secrets, and pinning ports only on the machine that wrote them is not
# pinning them at all. See context/04_tools.md.
!.claude/launch.json

# AI-OS: completed Specs in archive/ are versioned. Only generated outputs are ignored.
# Add any repo-specific exclusions here.

# Vendored ECC plugin — never commit upstream VCS / build artifacts that
# may slip into vendor/ecc/ on future refreshes.
vendor/ecc/.git
vendor/ecc/node_modules
vendor/ecc/dist

# codex-plugin-cc vendored - internal git excluded
vendor/codex-plugin-cc/.git
vendor/codex-plugin-cc/node_modules
vendor/codex-plugin-cc/dist

# Python bytecode cache (never intentionally committed)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.grepai/

# Memory stack runtime data (FalkorDB graph + Ollama models) — regenerated by
# `docker compose up`, never versioned.
memory/falkordb/data/
memory/falkordb/ollama-data/

# plans-pipeline runtime state (per-machine cursor, not shared config).
apps/data/tools/plans-pipeline/state.json

# Per-agent enrichment scratch: the numbered/suffixed PROGRESS logs each loop agent writes,
# and agent working dirs. These only ever run on one machine, so they are noise in the shared
# history.
#
# They live in apps/data/progress/ rather than at the repo root, beside the corpus the loop
# writes. The loop's whole 4-file set moved with them (TASK.md, LOOP_INSTRUCTIONS.md,
# PROGRESS.md, and the outputs dir), because that loop enriches the plans corpus and is not
# framework machinery. Its paths point at the new locations: leaving any of them pointing at
# the root would recreate the files upstairs on the next run and undo the move.
#
# Neither pattern matches bare `PROGRESS.md`, which is the tracked ai-os-loop convention file
# (the loop's memory across runs) and must stay in git — verified at its new path with
# `git check-ignore apps/data/progress/PROGRESS.md`.
apps/data/progress/PROGRESS.*.md
PROGRESS.*.md
_agent*/
